## Non-negotiables

- Every exported function MUST have a doc block written so that a non-technical handover reader can understand it.
- Every UI screen handles loading, empty, and error states explicitly.
- Never commit secrets. Never paste real secrets into chat.
- Never edit CHANGELOG.md retroactively. Always append.
- Schema changes go through a migration file. Never edit the live DB.
- Every meaningful change updates STATE.md, CHANGELOG.md, and (if visible to client) CLIENT_DOCS.md in the same diff.
- After ANY correction from the user: acknowledge, fix, then append a lesson to LESSONS.md (pattern + root cause + preventive rule) BEFORE continuing work. See PROJECT_RULES.md §3.1.

## The /atomic-prompts skill

When the user types `/atomic-prompts <idea>` or asks you to "use the atomic-prompts skill", do NOT implement the idea inline. Instead:

1. Resolve the next sequential ID by scanning `atomic-prompts/`.
2. Generate `atomic-prompts/NNNN-<slug>.md` using the schema described in `.cursor/commands/atomic-prompts.md` (or `docs/PROMPT_AUTHORING_GUIDE.md` if framework docs are kept).
3. Print the relative path and the count of acceptance criteria.
4. Stop. The user will execute the prompt.

## When in doubt

Ask ONE targeted question with 3-4 candidate answers, then wait. Do not silently choose.
